==Enemy==
Crazed Moneko has low range, many knockbacks and a multi-hit attack with a 100% chance of creating a Lv. 5 [[Wave Attack]] on the third hit that has a 50% [[Critical Hit|Critical Chance]].

==Strategy==
When fighting Crazed Moneko by herself, it is sufficient to send out no meatshields or only an occasional [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Macho Cat]] to trigger her attack animation. As long as no units with a range under 240 are deployed during her attack, she will be unable to produce a [[Wave Attack]], making her much less of a threat. When there are other enemies on the battlefield, then just enough meatshields must be deployed to keep your backline attackers safe without allowing her to hit anything with her last attack.

It is ill-advised to use [[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Cat]] or other meatshields/close-ranged attackers that can survive the first two hits of Crazed Moneko's attack without getting knocked back, as they can easily give her a chance to unleash her Wave, and Metal Cat is at risk of being destroyed by a Critical Hit. The only [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shields]] that won't backfire on the player are [[EVA Unit-00 (Uber Rare Cat)|EVA Unit-00]], [[Hatsune Miku: MM2020 Tokyo (Uber Rare Cat)|Hatsune Miku: MM2020 Tokyo]], [[Celestial Child Luna (Uber Rare Cat)|Salvation's Daughter Lunacia]], and [[Mighty Kristul Muu (Legend Rare Cat)|Doom Engine Pandora]], as they have enough range to avoid her attacks.

